## Execution Profiles — proportional orchestration

This section overrides any older wording that makes the Full Council workflow
the default after this skill is loaded.

`EXECUTION_PROFILE=AUTO | DIRECT | LIGHT | FULL` controls orchestration.
`AUTO` always starts from `DIRECT`; after targeted context, the orchestrating
model may raise the profile. File count, task length, a theoretical edge case,
or a Medium/Low finding are never sufficient reasons by themselves.

Use the optional helper to keep the narrow deterministic safety floor visible
without transferring normal engineering judgment out of the model:

```bash
python3 .harness/lib/council_profile.py --input-json '<json>'
```

### DIRECT — default for clear, local, reversible work

Do **not** start `council_session.py`. Do not create Context Delivery receipts,
execution graphs, subagents, review loops, or per-item commits merely because
the Council skill was mentioned.

Keep only:

```text
OBJECTIVE: observable result
DONE-WHEN: concrete validation
NON-GOALS: scope that must not expand
```

Then inspect only the necessary context, execute, validate with real commands,
and deliver. Escalate only when new evidence materially changes risk or scope.

### LIGHT — compact Council for non-trivial but reversible work

Do **not** start the enforceable Full Council state machine and do not require
formal Context Delivery. Preserve the objective and use one compact plan rather
than phase-plan + item-plan for every micro-step:

```text
OBJECTIVE
DONE-WHEN
CONTEXT-SUMMARY
PLAN: 3-7 ordered steps
EXECUTE
VALIDATE
CONSOLIDATED-REVIEW
DELIVER + BACKLOG
```

Use at most two subagents and only for genuinely independent work. One
consolidated review is enough by default; at most one targeted recheck follows
a real blocking fix. Do not require one local commit per micro-slice.

`CRITICAL`/`HIGH` findings reachable in the current task are `FIX_NOW`.
Medium/Low or unreachable findings go to execution backlog and do not block
delivery.

### FULL — high-assurance exception

Only `FULL` activates the existing enforceable Council lifecycle, Context
Delivery (when enabled), graph/test binding, persisted transitions and strict
review evidence. Use it when the user asks for Full/high-assurance execution or
when evidence shows a material floor such as:

- production/deploy;
- destructive or irreversible action;
- data migration/backfill with material risk;
- security/privacy/credential boundary;
- irreversible business decision.

The model may also choose FULL for a genuinely high-risk case and must state
the concrete evidence that justified escalation.

### Escalation policy

```text
AUTO -> DIRECT
DIRECT -> LIGHT   when targeted context proves broader coordination is useful
LIGHT  -> FULL    only when material high-assurance risk is evidenced
```

Before the first mutation, the model may also downgrade if exploration proves
the task is narrower than initially assumed.

Never optimize for zero findings. Optimize for the requested outcome with zero
reachable Critical/High blockers; record the rest in backlog.
